      "groupEmoji": "🏗️",
      "level": "ADVANCED",
      "html": "<div>\n\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"ct-hero\"><h2>Break of Structure & Change of Character 💥</h2><p>BOS and CHOCH are the two most important signals in Smart Money Concepts (SMC). They tell you whether the trend is CONTINUING or REVERSING. Master these and you'll never be on the wrong side of a big move again.</p></div>\n\n    <h3>💥 BOS — Break of Structure</h3>\n    <p>A <span class=\"ct-keyword\">BOS (Break of Structure)</span> happens when price breaks BEYOND a previous structural high (in an uptrend) or structural low (in a downtrend). It CONFIRMS that the current trend is continuing.</p>\n    <div class=\"ct-callout ct-callout--analogy\"><div class=\"ct-callout-label\">🏃 Analogy</div><p>Imagine a runner setting a new personal best every race. Each new personal best = BOS. It confirms they're still getting faster (the trend continues).</p></div>\n\n    <h3>🔄 CHOCH — Change of Character</h3>\n    <p>A <span class=\"ct-keyword\">CHOCH (Change of Character)</span> happens when price breaks in the OPPOSITE direction of the current trend for the FIRST TIME. It signals that the trend may be REVERSING.</p>\n\n    <svg width=\"100%\" height=\"310\" viewBox=\"0 0 720 310\">\n      <text x=\"360\" y=\"22\" fill=\"#f0b429\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">BOS vs CHOCH — Trend Continuation then Reversal</text>\n\n      <!-- Price path: uptrend with BOS, then CHOCH -->\n      <polyline points=\"40,260 90,220 120,238 170,185 200,200 250,150 280,165 330,110 360,128 400,85 430,100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3fb950\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"0\"/>\n      <!-- CHOCH: first break of a HL -->\n      <polyline points=\"430,100 480,155 510,130 560,190 590,160 650,230\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f85149\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n\n      <!-- BOS markers on uptrend -->\n      <line x1=\"170\" y1=\"185\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#3fb950\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n      <text x=\"170\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#3fb950\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BOS ✅</text>\n      <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#3fb950\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n      <text x=\"250\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#3fb950\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BOS ✅</text>\n      <line x1=\"330\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#3fb950\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n      <text x=\"330\" y=\"292\" fill=\"#3fb950\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BOS ✅</text>\n\n      <!-- CHOCH marker -->\n      <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#f85149\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/>\n      <rect x=\"455\" y=\"288\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"rgba(248,81,73,.2)\" stroke=\"rgba(248,81,73,.5)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"480\" y=\"299\" fill=\"#f85149\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">CHOCH ⚠️</text>\n\n      <!-- Labels on chart -->\n      <text x=\"200\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#3fb950\" font-size=\"10\">Bullish Structure (HH+HL)</text>\n      <text x=\"560\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#f85149\" font-size=\"10\">Bearish shift begins</text>\n      <line x1=\"440\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#bc8cff\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4\"/>\n      <text x=\"440\" y=\"60\" fill=\"#bc8cff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Transition point</text>\n\n      <!-- HL broken annotation -->\n      <text x=\"520\" y=\"125\" fill=\"#f85149\" font-size=\"9\">Previous HL broken!</text>\n      <text x=\"480\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#f85149\" font-size=\"9\">Now making LH</text>\n    </svg>\n\n    <h3>⚡ The Critical Difference</h3>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th></th><th>BOS</th><th>CHOCH</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>Direction</td><td>Same as current trend</td><td>Opposite to current trend</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Meaning</td><td>Trend CONTINUES</td><td>Trend may be REVERSING</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Action</td><td>Look for continuation trades</td><td>Stop looking for trend trades — look for reversal</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Confirmation needed?</td><td>BOS alone = valid signal</td><td>CHOCH = warning; wait for follow-through</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <div class=\"ct-callout ct-callout--warn\"><div class=\"ct-callout-label\">⚠️ Common Mistake</div><p>Not every CHOCH leads to a full reversal. Price can CHOCH and then continue the original trend (a \"liquidity sweep\"). Always wait for at least one BOS in the new direction after a CHOCH before committing to a reversal trade.</p></div>\n\n    <!-- QUIZ: BOS/CHOCH -->\n\n\n    <!-- HOMEWORK: BOS/CHOCH -->\n    <div>\n      <div>📝 Homework — BOS & CHOCH Identification</div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Chart Task</div>\n        <div>Task 1 — BOS Hunt (30 min)</div>\n        <p>On TradingView, open BTC/USDT on the 4H chart. Go back 6 months. Using the line tool, mark every BOS (label it \"BOS ↑\" for bullish or \"BOS ↓\" for bearish) and every CHOCH (label \"CHOCH\"). Count how many BOS occurred before each CHOCH. What was the average?</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div>Demo Trade</div>\n        <div>Task 2 — Paper Trade a CHOCH Setup (This week)</div>\n        <p>On your demo account (Bybit or Binance Testnet): Set an alert for when a CHOCH forms on any top-20 coin on the 1H chart. When triggered, wait for 1 BOS in the new direction, then enter a demo trade in that direction. Record the result. Goal: 5 CHOCH trades this week.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n\n  </div>\n</div>",
